{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T14:03:53.085751Z","id":"cdf205d42d48fc39bbcec3c20a61c161c8417f2d056048a2e9bba1381e66f5e5","body":{"detail":"`clax_bot::clax::Tally` is exported because `ClaxProvider::begin` in crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs (157-159) calls `Tally::of(cx.history)`. Inside the crate its readers are the tick (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs 1052) and crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs 217 and 554. It is the crate's own integration test reading the crate's own type, so no crate turns on another's features and the layering is as it was; but it makes the provider's private fold part of what clax-server and clax-worker can name. When the `clax` provider lives in `crates/clax-bot/src/clax/` and the proof drives it instead of its own adapter, make `Tally`, its fields and `Tally::of` `pub(crate)`. The adapter's old fold and this one agree on every history the proof builds: asserted equal in `begin` with a temporary assertion (base and `created` from every step with a payload, against `Tally::of`), all of `//crates/clax-bot:all` passed. They differ only where a step that is not a script carries `created: true`, which no tick writes. The proof still fails without `created` (`seam::a_script_after_one_that_created_an_artifact_may_not_create_another`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"4b5d1115070aa2816829bdff9d21e8efb761960aedc557d8f3856e6f3f0662b1"},"summary":"`Tally` and its six fields are `pub` for one reader outside the crate, the proof's adapter in tests/seam.rs","tags":["t3","for-t5","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.584199Z","id":"be4a1e68494cbb3bf7aa07a8255211109e1e22fc75ebad670d922df8ccf095d4","body":{"detail":"The fold's readers are the tick (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs, `Tick::clax`) and `ClaxProvider::begin` (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs), which takes `base` and `created` from `Tally::of(cx.history)`. crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs has no adapter and names no `Tally`; `clax::tally` is a private module and `clax` exports `ClaxProvider` alone. `bazelisk build --config=clippy --output_groups=clippy_checks //crates/clax-bot/...` passes. Proposed close: fixed.","kind":"comment","references":"cdf205d42d48fc39bbcec3c20a61c161c8417f2d056048a2e9bba1381e66f5e5","summary":"`Tally` and `Tally::of` are `pub(crate)`: the provider that reads them is in this crate","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596247Z","id":"6f5a08aa3fc639961950f83934a437773526798f0288aa3a5b180a1d946e2a73","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is (it was record b7a2cda0c5f3fc510f0905fd7e9e21c0d97a64ef6bc36c1f1a8d743d0316f004 on crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs, a file that moved). A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":675},"end":{"line":700},"content_hash":"edb9dabc23726a743971332f3760e638b8beabcea31ae864c26caf366bbfc067"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","tags":["t5","revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596293Z","id":"c70dda80ac5e8d1e4a9ca1261383538ebf22eba7f6ff0b5b33018ecfe83f6887","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs still calls `BotHost::working` (before a turn or a script, and after each terminal commit) and posts every notice itself (`notify_at`). crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls no provider's `working`: row 1 of the step table in surface.rs says so. For the change that moves the endings: the run loop calls `working`, `ending` and `ended` for every binding; the conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs) then has an `ending` that can fail and notices to read, and the two cases it names as not applicable are played; and a run whose scripts reach another surface (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) still ends with Clax's notices on Clax's threads, because only its script step is generic.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"4bbea682b0fceba2dff6b9e5f9883525e18cb40bc5eff616f5d905b19fce3974"},"summary":"Clax's provider does nothing in `working`, `ending` and `ended`: the roster and the notices are still the run loop's","tags":["t5","for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596550Z","id":"f568a9a7148f4402ac45b96d2f7033d2b3ad22553343217c47d6f92290a3ca47","body":{"detail":"`api::Performer`: this match, by which a session finds the part that performs an operation; `host::check_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs), for a `BotHost`'s own check; the table and its tests in api.rs; and the reference. `Deps::host`: run.rs (the roster's `working`, the notices' `plan_reply`, the request's `context`), driver.rs (`start_waiting`) and `ClaxProvider::of`. `Deps::web`: `ClaxProvider::of` alone. A provider that names its own operations (a match on the operation's name here) frees `Performer`; `Deps::host` and `Deps::web` go when the tick is given its providers and the roster and notices are theirs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"3112b5ac304ee179058eedc91c555550952cae4eb53b7282672bc3915157f265"},"summary":"What still reads `api::Performer`, `Deps::host` and `Deps::web`","tags":["t5","for-t10","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596594Z","id":"785c9e30c896757cdde2a5925e67644cf602e520e4b17c7ebbbb7c8fdd4a85e8","body":{"detail":"Before, the web performer made the journal entry itself and, when it could not (`run_not_claimed`), answered with no `cost_milli`. Now the refusal is the run loop's to journal (`Answer::refused(…).uncharged()`), made before any entry is, so its `call` event carries `cost_milli: 0` whether or not the row could be written. The attempt is abandoned either way (the claim is lost), no step commits it, and no test reaches it: crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs loses no claim. Keeping the old event would cost a read of the run for each such refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"A refusal of check 2 made while the driver no longer holds the run shows a cost of 0 in its event, where the code before the seam showed none","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:52:12.563931Z","id":"7b719df59cc1d709cda14e1c9433fd90f7a39dfa7e68140fa4d3dda0fc7766d0","body":{"detail":"A sandbox that lets another driver take the run before the script's first call, with a script that calls `clax.web.fetch` in a run that did not declare `fetch`, and in one that declared it on a host with no source (a test added to a scratch copy of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs). The reference's `call` event: `{\"code\":\"run_not_claimed\",\"ok\":false,\"op\":\"web.fetch\",\"ms\":0,\"web\":{\"url\":…}}`, no `cost_milli`. The seam's: `{\"code\":\"web_disabled\",\"cost_milli\":0,…}`. Both for both halves of check 2; no journal row either way; both ticks end `Waiting(NotOurs)`. The reason is in crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference/web.rs 464-472: the reference made the journal entry before it looked at whether the refusal was check 2's, and answered the entry's failure. So the script's own `catch` sees another code too, and the sentence in crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs 163-166 (\"shows `cost_milli: 0` … where the code before the seam … showed no cost\") and \"What the script is thrown … did not change\" (159-161) hold only while the driver has the run. Who can see it: someone with the run's panel open on the live stream (`EventHub::emit` broadcasts an attempt's events as they are made, crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs 272-310) sees that call until the next attempt's `step_started` replaces the step; nothing stores it, no step commits it, and the model is never told. The entry also fails when the read of the run's row fails (`Store::call_entry`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs 1498) with the claim held: then the step does commit, with `web_disabled` in its `calls` and in what the model is told where it had the store's error. To make it identical: `ClaxSession::web` makes the entry before check 2 and answers `unwritten` when it cannot (the read the reference made too), which covers the declared half; the undeclared half is answered by `SurfaceProvider::undeclared`, which is given no claim, so the core would have to make an entry before it asks the hook. The other refusals of the core (arguments that do not hold) were always answered as themselves whatever the entry did (crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs 365-374), so the seam's answer is the consistent one.","kind":"comment","references":"785c9e30c896757cdde2a5925e67644cf602e520e4b17c7ebbbb7c8fdd4a85e8","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"Reproduced, and it is more than the cost: the script is answered `web_disabled` where the code before the seam answered `run_not_claimed`","tags":["verify-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:15.997719Z","id":"669d3cf55974a761a785f19f29e64ee3127e1ba68eeecbd8e2b3ec953591d899","body":{"detail":"`clax_bot::clax::Tally` is exported because `ClaxProvider::begin` in crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs (157-159) calls `Tally::of(cx.history)`. Inside the crate its readers are the tick (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs 1052) and crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs 217 and 554. It is the crate's own integration test reading the crate's own type, so no crate turns on another's features and the layering is as it was; but it makes the provider's private fold part of what clax-server and clax-worker can name. When the `clax` provider lives in `crates/clax-bot/src/clax/` and the proof drives it instead of its own adapter, make `Tally`, its fields and `Tally::of` `pub(crate)`. The adapter's old fold and this one agree on every history the proof builds: asserted equal in `begin` with a temporary assertion (base and `created` from every step with a payload, against `Tally::of`), all of `//crates/clax-bot:all` passed. They differ only where a step that is not a script carries `created: true`, which no tick writes. The proof still fails without `created` (`seam::a_script_after_one_that_created_an_artifact_may_not_create_another`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"1521962e2743a77a0bace237b50a13bcf0bb67403f6f9430723d168fa81330cb"},"summary":"`Tally` and its six fields are `pub` for one reader outside the crate, the proof's adapter in tests/seam.rs","supersedes":"cdf205d42d48fc39bbcec3c20a61c161c8417f2d056048a2e9bba1381e66f5e5","tags":["t3","for-t5","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:16.225004Z","id":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","body":{"detail":"Before, the web performer made the journal entry itself and, when it could not (`run_not_claimed`), answered with no `cost_milli`. Now the refusal is the run loop's to journal (`Answer::refused(…).uncharged()`), made before any entry is, so its `call` event carries `cost_milli: 0` whether or not the row could be written. The attempt is abandoned either way (the claim is lost), no step commits it, and no test reaches it: crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs loses no claim. Keeping the old event would cost a read of the run for each such refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"A refusal of check 2 made while the driver no longer holds the run shows a cost of 0 in its event, where the code before the seam showed none","supersedes":"785c9e30c896757cdde2a5925e67644cf602e520e4b17c7ebbbb7c8fdd4a85e8","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:16.456886Z","id":"285218bc68466d1025cdd5d54e4571cd8f62d9458686a10d0f42b5f2e46ef010","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is (it was record b7a2cda0c5f3fc510f0905fd7e9e21c0d97a64ef6bc36c1f1a8d743d0316f004 on crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs, a file that moved). A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":678},"end":{"line":703},"content_hash":"edb9dabc23726a743971332f3760e638b8beabcea31ae864c26caf366bbfc067"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","supersedes":"6f5a08aa3fc639961950f83934a437773526798f0288aa3a5b180a1d946e2a73","tags":["t5","revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:22.680124Z","id":"454b9a36fdb17df4f5061f4bb91bdfe8dc701aee7df51a9cf58fb614bd2981c4","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record 7564590a4493710cb151474667f770e3c09df7943ba45796371ac003bf16eaed on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":147},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"6d8ae587df767f4b4d0cb20618cf56c2ea4b0ef14a847a74dc2598a4cbb0cef3"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:24.083263Z","id":"70a0f3e01dc4e6ae5a75116d137c99e1f6dc440621ac28e2f465d3c652966eb8","body":{"detail":"It decides whether a web call's audit record keeps the provider's response whole or by hash. It bounds no run and the model reads none of it, so it is not among `RunLimits` (crates/clax-bot/src/policy.rs:91); it is a limit of the web surface's own, and moves with the web performer.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record f7cbc515f60afe885145fd0d4c2ef407c88e89a5dbb4403361691a3f20514979 on crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"d92a55cc832e824030ea87b64f387e29c4f8a17a1dcc1e218747e9551542fc47"},"summary":"`AUDIT_RESPONSE_BYTES` (64 KiB) is a size compiled into the web performer","tags":["for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:56.201507Z","id":"9d48f43bcaa15c28c3a7528ee441c79a4058e07ce5aca0e2e177adbbe95ce65c","body":{"detail":"A sandbox that lets another driver take the run before the script's first call, with a script that calls `clax.web.fetch` in a run that did not declare `fetch`, and in one that declared it on a host with no source (a test added to a scratch copy of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs). The reference's `call` event: `{\"code\":\"run_not_claimed\",\"ok\":false,\"op\":\"web.fetch\",\"ms\":0,\"web\":{\"url\":…}}`, no `cost_milli`. The seam's: `{\"code\":\"web_disabled\",\"cost_milli\":0,…}`. Both for both halves of check 2; no journal row either way; both ticks end `Waiting(NotOurs)`. The reason is in crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference/web.rs 464-472: the reference made the journal entry before it looked at whether the refusal was check 2's, and answered the entry's failure. So the script's own `catch` sees another code too, and the sentence in crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs 163-166 (\"shows `cost_milli: 0` … where the code before the seam … showed no cost\") and \"What the script is thrown … did not change\" (159-161) hold only while the driver has the run. Who can see it: someone with the run's panel open on the live stream (`EventHub::emit` broadcasts an attempt's events as they are made, crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs 272-310) sees that call until the next attempt's `step_started` replaces the step; nothing stores it, no step commits it, and the model is never told. The entry also fails when the read of the run's row fails (`Store::call_entry`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs 1498) with the claim held: then the step does commit, with `web_disabled` in its `calls` and in what the model is told where it had the store's error. To make it identical: `ClaxSession::web` makes the entry before check 2 and answers `unwritten` when it cannot (the read the reference made too), which covers the declared half; the undeclared half is answered by `SurfaceProvider::undeclared`, which is given no claim, so the core would have to make an entry before it asks the hook. The other refusals of the core (arguments that do not hold) were always answered as themselves whatever the entry did (crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs 365-374), so the seam's answer is the consistent one.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"Reproduced, and it is more than the cost: the script is answered `web_disabled` where the code before the seam answered `run_not_claimed`","supersedes":"7b719df59cc1d709cda14e1c9433fd90f7a39dfa7e68140fa4d3dda0fc7766d0","tags":["verify-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:16:38.552330Z","id":"764a6add48725e68941adf2f99fd3f5b0282a054b4dc99e72792b67542ad154d","body":{"detail":"Kept: a refusal the run loop can make without the store is made without it. crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs (\"When the entry cannot be made, the answer itself differs\") states both cases. (1) Another driver holds the run: the script is thrown `web_disabled` and the live `call` event shows that code and `cost_milli: 0`, where the code before the seam threw and showed `run_not_claimed` with no cost; nothing is journaled or committed and the tick waits `NotOurs`. Pinned by `web::a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_when_the_claim_is_lost` (crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs, both halves of check 2) and, as the second named exception in the header of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, by `a_refusal_at_check_2_is_made_without_the_store`, which holds the reference to its event and the seam to its own. Changed one at a time: the refusal with no cost shown fails `golden::web::the_journal_rows_of_web_operations_a_run_lacks_are_pinned`, `script_differential::a_refusal_at_check_2_is_made_without_the_store` and 5 more; the session making the entry before check 2 and answering its failure fails `script_differential::a_refusal_at_check_2_is_made_without_the_store`, `web::a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_when_the_claim_is_lost`. (2) The store fails to read the run's row while the driver holds the run (`Store::call_entry`): the step commits with `web_disabled` and `cost_milli: 0` in its `calls` and in what the model is told, where it committed the store's error, and the refusal has no row. Not pinned: `clax_store::Store` has no way for a test to make one read fail (no fault hook; removing the run's row fails the commit too). Pinning it takes a store that a test can make fail one read, which belongs with the change that gives the tick its providers. The owner's to confirm: this is the second place this step changes something a person can observe, beside the journal row of record 964e0fd9.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","summary":"Both cases are stated, the lost claim is pinned on the product path and as a named exception of the comparison, and the committed case cannot be driven: for the owner, the second observable change of this step","tags":["t5","fix-round","status:needs-decision","for-t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:45:38.105865Z","id":"e9eaa9fb6021e03f93353642746adfee58b30c62c74466e44a3120f9630b74f8","body":{"detail":"A sandbox whose host, around the script's first call, lets another driver take the run (clock forward 61 seconds, `Store::claim_run` by a new driver) and after the call takes it back for the tick's own driver (61 seconds more, `claim_run` again). The journal entry of that call cannot be made (`run_not_claimed`), and the step then commits, since the driver holds the run again and no one began the step meanwhile. Run in a scratch copy of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs at 65a77a602, with a script that calls `clax.web.fetch` and returns what it caught, for a run that did not declare `fetch` and for one that declared it on a host with no source. The reference's committed step: `calls: [{\"code\":\"run_not_claimed\",\"ok\":false,\"op\":\"web.fetch\",…}]` with no `cost_milli`, and the model is told `[\"run_not_claimed\",\"driver drv_… does not hold run …; claim it again\"]`. The seam's: `code: web_disabled`, `cost_milli: 0`, and the model is told `[\"web_disabled\",\"clax.web.fetch is not available to this run\"]`. No journal row either way. So the decided answer is what a model is told in the one case where a step commits it, and it is the better one: the reference told the model a driver's ID. crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs `a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_when_the_claim_is_lost` (1612) pins the attempt that is abandoned; the committed one is unpinned.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"suggested_fix":"Add the committed case beside that test with the sandbox above, asserting the step's `calls` entry and what the model is told.","summary":"The case that commits can be driven with the test store, with no fault hook: the claim taken and taken back within the one call","tags":["verify-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:52:39.873904Z","id":"34796d01db522ed3533bf1486c1b504ff22153f1b80a444f73b1c14b5c1a8203","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs, `a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_in_a_step_that_commits`: a sandbox whose host lets another driver take the run around the script's first call and takes it back for the tick's driver after (`LosesTheRunForACall`), for a fetch the run did not declare and for one it declared on a host with no source. The step commits with `calls: [{op: web.fetch, ok: false, code: web_disabled, cost_milli: 0, web: {url}}]`, the script's value is `[\"web_disabled\", \"clax.web.fetch is not available to this run\"]`, and the step has no journal row. crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, `a_refusal_at_check_2_is_committed_as_itself`, holds the reference to what it committed in the same run (`run_not_claimed`, no cost, a message that begins `driver drv_`) and the seam to its own. crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs (\"When the entry cannot be made\") and the comparison's header say so. `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:all --runs_per_test=3` passes. Still for the owner: whether this answer, the second thing this step changes that a person or a model can observe, stands.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","summary":"The step that commits the refusal is pinned, on the product path and in the comparison, by the method of reply e9eaa9fb; what is left undriven is a read of the run's row failing with the claim never lost","tags":["t5","fix-round","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T18:44:21.881501Z","id":"12824206ce6bdc39405aef25f774c3ce53beb68db6964ad921545921f642e73f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs: `show_working` and `run_ended` call `BotHost::working`, `run_ending` posts the notices (`post`, at `StepCx::notice` places, each a `plan_reply` run with `Claim::entry`), applies the finish rule over `Tally::of(cx.history)` and reads the sources. The run loop calls the three hooks for every binding (crates/clax-bot/src/ending.rs, `Tick::working`, `Tick::end`). The conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs, `claxs_own_provider_passes_the_provider_conformance_suite`) now plays the terminal cases: its `noticed` probe reads the journal rows at the terminal step's notice places and the replies in the store, an `ending` armed to fail after it posted is made again, and a fake beside the provider records the hooks for `lifecycle`; one case is left as not applicable (the unwritten failure). The notice is on the thread once after `ending` was called for four attempts, and `ended` told twice turns the roster off twice and changes no reply. A run whose one surface is the fake's (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) ends with no reply on a thread and no call to the host: `a_run_of_the_fake_alone_finishes`, `_gives_up`, `_is_cancelled`, `_is_stopped_by_a_cap`, `_fails`.","kind":"comment","references":"c70dda80ac5e8d1e4a9ca1261383538ebf22eba7f6ff0b5b33018ecfe83f6887","summary":"Clax's provider now does the roster, the notices, the finish rule, the sources and the follow-ups in `working`, `ending` and `ended`","tags":["t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T18:44:21.885295Z","id":"02eec7eb4f4d4800d66e49fddbf35c2e0e7549d020237d52ed80306adb7fd225","body":{"detail":"The notice of thread `i` is journaled at the same place whatever the end (`StepCx::notice(i)`), and a step begun again keeps its number. A `stopped` or `give_up` step that posted its notice and then could not be committed `max_commit_failures` times becomes the `failed` step under the same number: the `failed` notice is another call at a place the journal holds, and is refused there. Seen with the fake, whose `ending` answers `key_reused` (`generic::an_ending_that_fails_is_counted_and_bounded_and_the_other_binding_is_still_asked`); for `clax` the entry is made by `Claim::entry` over `Store::call_entry` and was not driven here, and it was the same before the endings moved (the run loop posted both at `NOTICE_SEQ + i`). The thread then holds the first notice and the run ends `failed` with the failure's words in its payload only. No golden covers a terminal step whose commit fails after its notice was posted (the `failed` goldens fail a script step, which posts none).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"6637c0fcf6ea434dde7cce6a059ab9d29965d82f8d6efcd79d6c414f6f3bd0e1"},"summary":"A terminal step that ends as another kind than its earlier attempts keeps their notice places, so its notice may be refused the key and not posted","tags":["t7","for-t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:38:58.352682Z","id":"dbd92c1402d4bf20dcf666adbf9a28305bf5e3c738bed97eb977176d3c94a636","body":{"detail":"`posted` is set from the rule alone (line 202), as the run loop did before the move (crates/clax-bot/src/ending_reference.rs 223, 241) and as crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs's table says (`posted` is true whenever the rule held, whether or not a post succeeded). Changing line 202 to `json!(post && every post succeeded)` (each `self.post` returning whether all its replies were made) passes `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all`: no golden or comparison run has a finish whose summary post fails. The field is stored in the step's payload and nothing in the product reads it today, so a change there would be silent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"74a1d3a54c0ee1603e7f71b65cde3f599028c63d0cd36f92bca1d08d1439e2f7"},"suggested_fix":"A `finish` on two threads whose second reply cannot be planned (move the thread off the run's artifact, as the review probe did with `UPDATE threads SET artifact_id` under `PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF`), pinning `posted: true` and one reply.","summary":"No test holds that a finished step's `posted` is the finish rule whatever came of the posts","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:38:58.353476Z","id":"1296adde916cffa2ab552e5fbd8c0769c6847a9afca1d9410f0e2512f5a2d5c0","body":{"detail":"A probe test added to crates/clax-bot/src/ending_differential.rs and removed after: a run on one thread with ClaxBot turned off, a SQLite trigger refusing the commit of any `stopped` step (`BEFORE UPDATE OF committed_at ON bot_steps WHEN OLD.kind = 'stopped'`), driven to its end both ways. Both end `failed`, the thread holds one reply (the stop's notice), and what the two leave (`Left`: run, steps, journal, events, audit, usage, writes, calls, replies, roster) is equal. `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test --test_arg=probe_` passed. The journal keys a reply by run, step and place, not attempt (crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs `with_bot_journal`), before the move and after it.","kind":"comment","references":"02eec7eb4f4d4800d66e49fddbf35c2e0e7549d020237d52ed80306adb7fd225","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"6637c0fcf6ea434dde7cce6a059ab9d29965d82f8d6efcd79d6c414f6f3bd0e1"},"summary":"Driven for `clax`: a `failed` step after a posted stop notice posts nothing of its own, through the seam and through the reference alike","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:07:27.532403Z","id":"7fdbd3471c874a7f9d9454da0177a221594d23166e32b9682e9275b39a0a064a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"02eec7eb4f4d4800d66e49fddbf35c2e0e7549d020237d52ed80306adb7fd225","summary":"Not changed by holding the run's `RunInfo` and providers: the notice places are the binding's and the step's number, which did not move; still open","tags":["t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:07:27.532734Z","id":"84923db596ebf1f981e94963644b0f84b220270dd85a44f7f05492c2c617f5ca","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","summary":"Not changed: the web session and its refusals were not touched by the tick holding its providers; still for the owner","tags":["t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T23:59:19.585787Z","id":"5c41a158fbcbf6646a6b618b93366aacf7c753057742999ad3523fa3f9feeb23","body":{"detail":"Commits ac72d8527 and 359f0c1f4; see the reply on record d311ae86 (crates/clax-bot/src/registry.rs). `host::host_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs) checks that the operation is one of src/clax.d.ts with the access asked. Left open for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"f568a9a7148f4402ac45b96d2f7033d2b3ad22553343217c47d6f92290a3ca47","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"7c64c4ec37072d9b071617065da0502686ca4854cd798312e8cffe6eb54bbaa4"},"summary":"Done: the session names its own operations (`PARTS`, `Part`), and `api::Performer`, `Deps.host` and `Deps.web` are gone","tags":["t10","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:03.325472Z","id":"f6bc4e8fec82aa61650c6347e56085d7883e14c313a264c3dbd60876e980a10c","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record 7564590a4493710cb151474667f770e3c09df7943ba45796371ac003bf16eaed on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"6d8ae587df767f4b4d0cb20618cf56c2ea4b0ef14a847a74dc2598a4cbb0cef3"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","supersedes":"454b9a36fdb17df4f5061f4bb91bdfe8dc701aee7df51a9cf58fb614bd2981c4","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:03.498738Z","id":"605dcd1c00f980ef5797e5a87538ef7afa971998e2db061f0dacd722b67c93f0","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs still calls `BotHost::working` (before a turn or a script, and after each terminal commit) and posts every notice itself (`notify_at`). crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls no provider's `working`: row 1 of the step table in surface.rs says so. For the change that moves the endings: the run loop calls `working`, `ending` and `ended` for every binding; the conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs) then has an `ending` that can fail and notices to read, and the two cases it names as not applicable are played; and a run whose scripts reach another surface (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) still ends with Clax's notices on Clax's threads, because only its script step is generic.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"b98a54081114280cbb82dee794235753f257b363e8a6fd67bdb34ad194813be2"},"summary":"Clax's provider does nothing in `working`, `ending` and `ended`: the roster and the notices are still the run loop's","supersedes":"c70dda80ac5e8d1e4a9ca1261383538ebf22eba7f6ff0b5b33018ecfe83f6887","tags":["t5","for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:03.668669Z","id":"8320f2cf8d7130eda31cd5a453323a0ae3f6a7b060213b2cdbc71aab3002f540","body":{"detail":"`api::Performer`: this match, by which a session finds the part that performs an operation; `host::check_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs), for a `BotHost`'s own check; the table and its tests in api.rs; and the reference. `Deps::host`: run.rs (the roster's `working`, the notices' `plan_reply`, the request's `context`), driver.rs (`start_waiting`) and `ClaxProvider::of`. `Deps::web`: `ClaxProvider::of` alone. A provider that names its own operations (a match on the operation's name here) frees `Performer`; `Deps::host` and `Deps::web` go when the tick is given its providers and the roster and notices are theirs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"bf1684f5785655048d7101e7c4e6fa8a75f9e20c1bff1d031c3c83cd8072c39e"},"summary":"What still reads `api::Performer`, `Deps::host` and `Deps::web`","supersedes":"f568a9a7148f4402ac45b96d2f7033d2b3ad22553343217c47d6f92290a3ca47","tags":["t5","for-t10","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:15.715113Z","id":"8d9526d05ac474387a3a423118d738f9919e267082bbf4aa2b62dec38e84431c","body":{"detail":"`stop_lead` has a notice for each: 'this Clax could not work out what this run may do', 'this Clax could not put together what to send the model', 'the model took longer to answer than this run allows'. The first two end the run `failed`, the third `stopped`. None is reachable under `DefaultPolicy` (no fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden changes), and none is pinned by a fixture; the run view and the HTTP run JSON show `reason` as they show any. When the endings move behind a provider's `ending`, these reasons go with `End::Failed` and `End::Stopped` and the words become the provider's; whoever first ships such a policy pins them.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 23d65d69 on crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":75},"content_hash":"200a2a2652746f83ba212641529e22974fa196fc37d7e28c7544d872bee2eb6a"},"summary":"Three endings a person can see only under a policy that is not the default, with words nobody chose: `policy_error`, `policy_history_<n>` and `model_timeout`","tags":["for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:16.727657Z","id":"cdc6baabf39228a966f9c1cd77f434e0562a00999bc0410a694188b12d3dd008","body":{"detail":"`what_i_did` (1374-1396) reads `clax.scripts`, `clax.changed` and `clax.published`; `finish` reads `clax.replied` (1574). They are the only readers of those four `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), so when the notices and the posting rule move into the provider's `ending`, it folds `Tally::of(cx.history)` there and these reads go. `scripts` is in the tally although a script step is the core's and docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-11-claxbot-surfaces-step2.md (\"Where the nouns are read\", Core) lists it with the core's fields: its one reader is the notice's wording (\"I ran 2 scripts\"), and `history::Control` (crates/clax-bot/src/history.rs 86-99) holds only what the tick decides by. A provider that is not `clax` and wants the count folds it from the steps' kinds. Held: `clax: Tally::default()` at run.rs 1052 fails 25 integration tests, `golden::endings::a_notice_counts_the_scripts_that_ran` among them; 1574 without `replied` fails `golden::endings::finish_posts_no_summary_on_any_thread_when_the_run_replied_on_one`.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record e90edb8f on crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"1657820bb3b6071503997d51979097102a92b417e031f6d7063baeb5d98d06c0"},"summary":"For the change that moves the endings behind `ending`: `what_i_did` and the finish rule read `Tick::clax`, and the count of scripts is in the tally, not in the core's fold","tags":["t3","for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:20.246630Z","id":"e44906117bbe90a86bb17433bc01292276a818fb96139ae002e39205a37647e2","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 7564590a on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"6b3ae9ea2f79eb1ad2baa17775c07b4ff2f4187e34a0a23f16d8632096698d61"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.928027Z","id":"b8e71a2cec89ce672794e3030882a91f62d4301879f4eaf4b67834ba96d79318","body":{"detail":"Every script the proof runs is step 2 of its run, after one turn: `tally` (seam.rs 102-111) always answers `(None, false)` and `begin` (145-163) always loads the draft at the run's own base. Changes made one at a time and run with `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` (7 tests): (1) seam.rs 148 loads the draft at `run.base_version` whatever `tally` answers: all 7 pass. (2) seam.rs 238 drops `self.created_before`: all 7 pass. (3) seam.rs 320 never refuses a second publish in one script: all 7 pass. (4) seam.rs 215 hands `OpCtx::new` another attempt: all 7 pass (the fake host does not read it; crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs 633 does). The same changes made to today's code and run against the whole of `//crates/clax-bot:integration` (175 tests): script.rs 217 without `self.tick.hist.created` fails `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused` and `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact`; script.rs 301 fails `golden::scripts::the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned`; but script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` passes all 175, the seam's 7 among them, and passes `//crates/clax-bot:all`, `//crates/clax-server:all` and `//crates/clax-worker:bot_test` too. No test runs a script after a step that published or rebased: crates/clax-bot/tests/rules.rs 143-197 rebases and publishes in the run's last script. So the change that moves script.rs 554-555 into a provider's `begin` can load every later script's draft at the run's first base (a second publish then conflicts, and a script after a rebase reads the old files) and pass the proof and every fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 487f98c0 on crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"6e87a4939198b0a2f01dfb9625d7c55ecf0b5ef98da47adfe2e665538ec87d3d"},"suggested_fix":"A proof case, and a fixture for today's path, in which a first script publishes (and another in which it rebases) and a second script reads a file, writes and publishes: the second step's draft, its `if_version` and its `payload.base` compared on both paths. For a brief's run, a second script that calls `artifacts.create` after a first that created one.","summary":"No proof case opens a session over a history that moved the draft's base or created an artifact, so what `begin` folds from the committed steps is unproved, and for the base no other test of clax-bot holds it either","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
